:0.223572,"roe":0.79255,"shares":137919000.0,"net_income":1234000000.0},{"fy_end":"2025-12-31","revenue":14733000000.0,"op_margin":0.126994,"eps":9.81,"fcf":3093270000.0,"owner_fcf":3093270000.0,"roic":0.410839,"roe":1.00779,"shares":131943000.0,"net_income":1294000000.0}],"hist_source":"SEC 10-K","hist_currency":"USD","profile":{"longBusinessSummary":"Expedia Group, Inc. operates as an online travel company in the United States and internationally. The company operates through B2C, B2B, and trivago segments. The B2C segment includes Brand Expedia, a full-service online travel brand offers various travel products and services; Hotels.com for lodging accommodations; Vrbo, an online marketplace for the alternative accommodations; and Orbitz, Travelocity, ebookers, and Wotif Group. The B2B segment provides various travel and non-travel companies including airlines, offline travel agents, online retailers, corporate travel management, and financial institutions who leverage its travel technology and tap into its diverse supply to augment their offerings and market Expedia Group rates and availabilities to its travelers. The trivago segment sends referrals to online travel companies and travel service providers from hotel metasearch websites. In addition, it provides brand advertising through online and offline channels, loyalty programs, mobile apps, and search engine marketing, as well as metasearch, social media, direct and personalized traveler communications on its websites, and through direct e-mail communication with its travelers. The company was formerly known as Expedia, Inc. and changed its name to Expedia Group, Inc. in March 2018. Expedia Group, Inc. was founded in 1996 and is headquartered in Seattle, Washington.","fullTimeEmployees":16000,"city":"Seattle","country":"United States","website":"https://www.expediagroup.com","industry":"Travel Services","sector":"Consumer Cyclical"},"news":[{"title":"Can Booking Holdings Stock Jump 40%?","link":"https://www.trefis.com/stock/bkng/articles/627219/can-booking-holdings-stock-jump-40-2/2026-11-20","publisher":"Trefis","date":"2026-11-20"},{"title":"BI Survey: Budgetary Constraints for 2027 Travel","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/video/bi-survey-budgetary-constraints-2027-175209454.html","publisher":"Bloomberg","date":"2026-11-20"},{"title":"What Is Airbnb Building That Investors Should Watch?","link":"https://www.trefis.com/stock/abnb/articles/626779/what-is-airbnb-building-that-investors-should-watch/2026-11-19","publisher":"Trefis","date":"2026-11-19"},{"title":"Can Booking Holdings Stock Rally 50% After This Dip?","link":"https://www.trefis.com/stock/bkng/articles/626681/can-booking-holdings-stock-rally-50-after-this-dip/2026-11-19","publisher":"Trefis","date":"2026-11-19"},{"title":"Will Raised Revenue Guidance Change Expedia's (EXPE) Narrative","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/raised-revenue-guidance-change-expedias-232429617.html","publisher":"Simply Wall St.","date":"2026-11-18"},{"title":"Should Booking Holdings Stock Investors Worry About Its Outlook?","link":"https://www.trefis.com/stock/bkng/articles/626220/should-booking-holdings-stock-investors-worry-about-its-outlook/2026-11-18","publisher":"Trefis","date":"2026-11-18"}],"info_date":"2026-11-21"}